 ('incal','The Incal issue 1 setting sidebar','Humanoids comic text indexed at Scribd','https://www.scribd.com/doc/269690694/The-Incal-01-Jodorowsky','indexed_comic_sidebar','City Shaft has stratified residents, aristocrats, a TechnoPope, Prez and robotic police.','Only the short indexed introductory sidebar; hierarchy and robot police do not establish household automatic provision.'),
 ('metabaron','The Metabaron reading diary','Ian Sales','https://iansales.com/category/reading-diary-2017/','secondary_review','The Techno-Techno Empire monopolizes the unique starship-fuel source.','A fuel monopoly and military machinery are not ordinary access to necessities.'),
 ('technopriests','The Technopriests','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Technopriests','secondary_plot_reference','Albino leads young technopriests toward a promised galaxy and narrates his rise.','A destination and liberation story do not establish its settled productive/access institutions.'),
 ('galaxity','Bad Dreams','Valerian and Laureline Wiki contributors','https://valerian-laureline.fandom.com/wiki/Bad_Dreams','secondary_album_reference','Work is abolished for most people and Dream Service programs support continuing leisure under technocrats.','Useful technical/security roles continue; dream users remain living residents, not dormant backups.'),
 ('alflolol','Welcome to Alflolol publisher synopsis reproduced in catalogue','Cinebook synopsis via Open Library','https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20051547W/Valerian_and_Laureline','publisher_synopsis_in_catalogue','Technorog is an industrial, agricultural and research center; indigenous return creates reinsertion conflict.','Industrial importance and colonial injustice do not establish an automated household floor.'),
 ('edena','The World of Edena','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_World_of_Edena','secondary_reference','Industrialized protagonists encounter natural food and transformed social/body relations.','Synthetic nutrition and religious symbolism do not establish the Paternum population’s distribution mechanism.'),
 ('yoko','Yoko Tsuno album summaries','Wikipedia contributors','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoko_Tsuno','secondary_album_reference','Central computer, Karpan engineering, returning Vineans and underwater tyranny occur in separate albums.','A rogue controller, a magma pipeline or nursery androids are not by themselves proof of a material floor.'),
