 ('c0775','technopriests','The promised Supra-Neutopian destination lacks verified settled resource institutions.','Leadership and a voyage toward liberation cannot be treated as an already implemented universal floor.'),
 ('c0777','alflolol','Technorog’s industry and indigenous reinsertion do not establish automatic ordinary allocation.','Research, agriculture and colonial coercion remain real material activity; Galaxity’s leisure is not copied to the industrial periphery.'),
 ('c0778','edena','The short Edena reference does not establish the Paternum society’s automatic access rules.','Body transformation, synthetic food themes and a godlike figure cannot substitute for a defined material mechanism.'),
 ('c0779','yoko','The Vinean central computer’s power does not establish ordinary work-independent necessities.','Control of a settlement and a computer conflict are not the same as productive/provision evidence.'),
 ('c0780','yoko','Karpan’s magma project does not establish a distinct automatic civilian economy.','A new-continent scheme and coercive leadership do not answer household allocation.'),
 ('c0781','vinea','Planetary maintenance and a survivor civilization do not establish labor-independent ordinary access.','Robot brains containing scientists’ memories are not automatically external AI; wind technology and fear do not supply a labor census.'),
 ('c0782','yoko','Underwater tyranny and rebellious androids do not establish ordinary productive allocation.','An ecological enclosure and robot opposition alone are insufficient.'),
 ('c0783','megalex','Megalex’s artificial city and disposable police clones lack a verified automatic necessities floor.','Biological clone enforcement is real human-derived work; addiction and royal lifespans do not prove post-work provision.')
